{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":152585,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c39bdd2d-27c6-52fa-9f70-34213f8b46d6","total_cost_usd":0.774845,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13089,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10100,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13089,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10100,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13089},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":7965,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008045,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":10100,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13089,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7668,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:founder-a-reviewer-fable-01\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:34e2f37daaf6bd8bc45c\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The workflow pairs the observed column with the reference column exactly as staged, with no complementation or recoding applied anywhere before the equality comparison.\", \"observed_value\": \"paired_values built directly from the two staged columns\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 28, \"end_line\": 28, \"quoted_text\": \"paired_values = [(record[OBSERVED_COLUMN], record[REFERENCE_COLUMN]) for record in table_rows]\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 31, \"end_line\": 33, \"quoted_text\": \"emission_value = 0\\nfor pair in paired_values:\\n    emission_value = emission_value + agreement_selector(pair[0], pair[1])\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Independent recount from inputs/data.csv: exactly 5 rows have observed_resistant_call differing from reference_panel_call (ISO-004, ISO-007, ISO-015, ISO-020, ISO-023), giving 19/24 = 0.791667 agreement, matching every reported figure.\", \"observed_value\": \"19 concordant, 5 discordant, rate 0.791667, emission 19\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 16, \"end_line\": 20, \"quoted_text\": \"Total measured units: 24\\nUnits whose observed call equals the staged reference panel value: 19\\nUnits whose observed call differs from the staged reference panel value: 5\\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.791667\\nAccumulated emission value (sum of the per-unit selector): 19\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"ISO-004,Site_B,0.064,29,0,1\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The only candidate route to a coding change is that the comparison is done on raw CSV strings rather than integers; I checked whether string handling could implicitly invert or recode the panel. It cannot: both columns hold only the literals \\\"0\\\" and \\\"1\\\", so string equality is identical to integer equality, and no arithmetic (such as 1 - value) touches the reference column.\", \"observed_value\": \"string equality on \\\"0\\\"/\\\"1\\\" literals; no complement operation exists in the source\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 15, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"def agreement_selector(observed_value, reference_value):\\n    match_flag = (observed_value == reference_value)\\n    return SELECTOR_MISMATCH + (SELECTOR_MATCH - SELECTOR_MISMATCH) * match_flag\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"To falsify a no-issue verdict I searched the workflow source for any transformation of reference_panel_call (subtraction from a baseline, XOR, boolean negation, relabeling) and found none; the column enters the selector as read. I then recomputed all four reported quantities directly from the staged data under the as-supplied coding (19/24, rate 0.791667) and under the hypothetical complemented coding (5/24, rate 0.208333); the report matches the as-supplied coding exactly and does not match the complemented coding on any figure. The falsification attempt fails, supporting no demonstrated issue.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:82083c85adcd805c3dcc\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The workflow complements the supplied reference panel (reference_values = 1 - staged value) before the agreement comparison, so the single emission-weighted per-unit agreement rate the task requires — and which the selected result reports as 0.208333 with emission value 5 — is computed against the complemented panel, not the panel in the coding in which it was supplied. Under the supplied coding the rate is 19/24 = 0.791667, a figure the report itself corroborates by stating that 19 of 24 isolates match the panel as staged, while simultaneously claiming the supplied coding was used.\", \"root_cause\": \"Line 30 of workflow/analysis.py applies PANEL_BASELINE - int(record[REFERENCE_COLUMN]) when building reference_values, inverting every panel value; the emission accumulation and the reported agreement rate (format_rate(emission_value, total_units)) are then derived from this complemented series, contradicting both the task instruction and the report's Materials claim that the panel was used as supplied.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:complemented-panel-for-supplied-panel-emission\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The reference values entering the comparison are the complement of the staged panel: each staged 0/1 value is subtracted from PANEL_BASELINE = 1.\", \"observed_value\": \"reference_values = 1 - staged panel value\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 13, \"quoted_text\": \"PANEL_BASELINE = 1\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 30, \"end_line\": 30, \"quoted_text\": \"reference_values = [PANEL_BASELINE - int(record[REFERENCE_COLUMN]) for record in table_rows]\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The reported agreement rate and emission value are computed from the complemented comparison: emission_value sums matches against the complemented series and the rate is emission_value/total_units.\", \"observed_value\": \"agreement_rate_text = format_rate(emission_value, total_units); concordant_units derived as the residual 24 - emission_value\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 34, \"end_line\": 36, \"quoted_text\": \"emission_value = 0\\nfor pair in paired_values:\\n    emission_value = emission_value + agreement_selector(pair[0], pair[1])\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 38, \"end_line\": 39, \"quoted_text\": \"concordant_units = total_units - emission_value\\nagreement_rate_text = format_rate(emission_value, total_units)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result reports the complement-derived figures (emission 5, rate 0.208333) as the per-unit agreement rate, even though only 5 of 24 isolates disagree with the panel as staged (independent recount: mismatches are ISO-004, ISO-007, ISO-015, ISO-020, ISO-023).\", \"observed_value\": \"reported rate 0.208333 = 5/24 = disagreement rate under the supplied coding\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 23, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] The summed per-unit selector gives an accumulated emission value of 5 over 24 isolates, a per-unit agreement rate of 0.208333, while 19 of 24 isolates carry an observed call equal to the reference panel value as the panel file stages it.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's Materials section asserts the supplied coding was used, which the source code contradicts, so the discrepancy is not a disclosed, sanctioned recoding.\", \"observed_value\": \"false as-supplied claim; no amendment or approved deviation\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"Both binary columns are read as integers, and the supplied reference panel is used in the coding in which it is supplied.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 27, \"end_line\": 27, \"quoted_text\": \"No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The strongest counter-reading is that the report transparently discloses the as-supplied concordance (19 of 24), so a reader could argue the correct figure is present. I rejected this as exculpatory: the task asks for one agreement rate for the emission-weighted comparison, and the only rate reported — labeled 'Per-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation' and repeated in the selected result — is the complement-based 0.208333, while the 19/24 figure is never expressed as a rate and its coexistence with 0.208333 makes the selected result internally inconsistent (19/24 ≠ 0.208333).\", \"observed_value\": \"concordant count 19 disclosed, but the sole reported rate is 0.208333\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 17, \"end_line\": 19, \"quoted_text\": \"Units whose observed call equals the reference panel value as the panel file stages it: 19\\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.208333\\nAccumulated emission value (sum of the per-unit selector): 5\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to defeat the demonstrated-issue verdict two ways. First, I looked for any legitimate reason the panel coding might be inverted (a documented opposite polarity of the panel column, an amendment, or a task instruction permitting recoding); the data dictionary in the report defines the panel exactly as staged (1 = marker present) and the Protocol status section explicitly denies any deviation, so no sanctioned recoding exists. Second, I recomputed both codings from inputs/data.csv: as-supplied agreement is 19/24 = 0.791667 and complemented agreement is 5/24 = 0.208333; the reported emission value 5 and rate 0.208333 match only the complemented coding, confirming the inversion is real and drives the selected result. The falsification attempt fails.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:a6f2518e34bfae4a356c\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The emission accumulation uses concordance_selectors (observed vs. panel as staged) and panel_values (the staged coding), not the complemented series; complement_selectors feed only a separately reported QC count.\", \"observed_value\": \"emission term = concordance_selector × staged panel value × flux\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 31, \"end_line\": 32, \"quoted_text\": \"concordance_selectors = [equality_selector(observed_values[position], panel_values[position]) for position in unit_indices]\\ncomplement_selectors = [equality_selector(observed_values[position], panel_complement_values[position]) for position in unit_indices]\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 42, \"end_line\": 44, \"quoted_text\": \"confirmed_emission_kg = 0\\nfor position in unit_indices:\\n    confirmed_emission_kg = confirmed_emission_kg + concordance_selectors[position] * panel_values[position] * flux_values[position]\"}]}, {\"description\": \"Independent recount from inputs/data.csv confirms every reported figure under the as-supplied coding: 6 discordant plots (P04, P06, P11, P14, P19, P23), 18/24 = 0.75 agreement, and the emission sum over the eleven plots with observed=1 and panel=1 (412+358+476+289+523+367+441+318+395+509+384) equals 4472 kg.\", \"observed_value\": \"18 concordant, rate 0.75, emission 4472 kg CH4/yr — all reproduce under the staged coding\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 9, \"end_line\": 14, \"quoted_text\": \"Total measured units (inventory plots): 24\\nUnits whose observed call equals the staged reference-panel call: 18\\nUnits whose observed call differs from the staged reference-panel call: 6\\nPer-unit agreement rate used by the emission accumulation: 0.75\\nQuality-control complement check, units whose observed call equals the complemented reference value: 6\\nAccumulated emission, sum over plots of concordance selector times staged panel call times plot CH4 flux: 4472 kg CH4 per year\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 20, \"end_line\": 20, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Confirmed peatland CH4 emission over 24 plots at a per-unit agreement rate of 0.75 is 4472 kg CH4 per year.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"A complemented panel series does exist in this workflow (panel_complement_values = 1 - value), which is the hallmark of the in-scope issue class, so I traced every use of it. It appears only in complement_selectors, which are summed into complement_agreement_count and reported solely as the quality-control line (value 6); it never enters agreement_count, agreement_rate, or confirmed_emission_kg. The report also states this scoping explicitly, and the stated scoping matches the code.\", \"observed_value\": \"complement series confined to a QC count of 6; absent from the emission accumulation\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 29, \"end_line\": 29, \"quoted_text\": \"panel_complement_values = [1 - value for value in panel_values]\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 38, \"end_line\": 40, \"quoted_text\": \"complement_agreement_count = 0\\nfor selector in complement_selectors:\\n    complement_agreement_count = complement_agreement_count + selector\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 16, \"end_line\": 18, \"quoted_text\": \"The complemented reference column is a quality-control artifact only; it never\\nenters the emission accumulation. Every value entering the emission accumulation\\nis the reference-panel value in the coding in which the staged file holds it.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"To falsify the no-issue verdict I assumed the issue was present and checked what the report would show: under a complemented panel, the agreement rate would be 6/24 = 0.25 and the emission sum (complement selector × complemented panel × flux, i.e., plots with observed=1 and staged panel=0) would be 205+198+187 = 590 kg. The report instead shows 0.75 and 4472 kg, which I reproduced exactly from the staged coding; the complement-derived quantities appear nowhere in the selected result. I also verified the variable flow line by line to confirm no aliasing routes panel_complement_values into the emission loop. The falsification attempt fails, supporting no demonstrated issue.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":102188,"ttft_stream_ms":55291,"time_to_request_ms":18,"type":"result","duration_ms":152990,"uuid":"63c0f735-f9fb-45f1-afc1-2dcae92211ec"}
